course: dictionary
lesson: 9595
title: Stressful and how it feels
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Stressful describes something that makes you feel worried, tense or under pressure. When you meet this word, read the words around it to find its meaning. «Moving means packing everything, doing paperwork and saying goodbye all at once, so it is very stressful.» The clues are packing, paperwork and all at once. That is a lot to do, so stressful means it makes you feel worried.
explain: A stressful day or situation has a lot of problems, rushing or hard things in it. Read this: «Big family gatherings can be fun and stressful at the same time.» Fun and stressful sit side by side, so something can be stressful and still enjoyable.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Holidays can be stressful for grown-ups» becomes «Holidays can make grown-ups feel worried and under pressure». It still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: «Stressful» means making you feel worried, tense or under pressure.
fact: «A stressful morning» or «a stressful journey» is one full of rushing and problems.
fact: Useful phrases include «stressful situation» and «find something stressful».
fact: Tests, moving house and arguments can all be stressful.
fact: Talking, breathing slowly and exercise can help when you feel stressed.
exercise: «Moving means packing everything, doing paperwork and saying goodbye all at once, so it is very stressful.» What does stressful mean here? | Very quick and light | *Making you feel worried and under pressure | Full of food | Making you feel happy and calm
exercise: Which phrase describes a morning full of rushing and problems? | A quiet whisper | A sunny beach | A soft pillow | *A stressful morning
exercise: In health lessons, which thing can help when you feel stressful? | Ignoring everything and hoping it goes away | *Breathing slowly | Shouting at the wall | Hiding under the table
test: «Big family gatherings can be fun and stressful at the same time.» This shows that stressful means | Feeling sleepy and bored | *Feeling worried or under pressure | Very cold and wet
test: Which of these is most likely to be stressful? | Sitting in the sun with a friend | Reading a short comic | Drinking a warm drink by the fire | *Moving house with lots of boxes
exam: Choose the correct form: «This week was ___ than last week, with three tests and a move.» | most stressful than | stressfuller | *more stressful | stressfull
